# Native implication audit

The tables record implications for comparisons on the stated mathematical
objects. The numeric identifiers also identify the labelled spectral forms
in `FirstAtlas.lean` and `SecondAtlas.lean`. Those forms allow arbitrary
evaluation of each sample. The rows with prefix C or S cover additional
operator comparisons and determinant reductions.

Read each arrow in the scope on its line. For a statement R, MOC → R gives
¬R → ¬MOC; R → MOC gives ¬MOC → ¬R. An iff transfers both proofs and
refutations. A restriction proved without MOC is not a reverse implication.
A stronger sufficient statement may fail without refuting MOC. “Open”,
“conditional”, and “math-only” are not checked proof declarations.

