C1 | Matrix form | LEAN_IFF | MOC.Reformulations.CStar.matrixForm_iff and scalarWeightForm_iff.
C2 | Orbit form | LEAN_IFF | MOC.Reformulations.CStar.orbitForm_iff; roots include algebraic multiplicities.
C3 | Commutant form | LEAN_IFF | MOC.Reformulations.commutantForm_iff; exact hull comparison. Lean reverse uses regular spectra plus density; joint diagonalization mathematically identifies the vertex sets even for repetitions.
C4 | Coupling (transport) form | LEAN_IFF | MOC.Reformulations.couplingForm_iff; integer transport tables of all label blocks (including repeated or empty labels) give exactly permutation vertices.
C5 | Cartesian form | LEAN_IFF | MOC.Reformulations.CStar.cartesianForm_iff in joint eigenbases; MOC.exists_joint_hermitian_diagonalization supplies joint bases for commuting Hermitian parts.
C6 | Functional calculus form | LEAN_IFF | MOC.Reformulations.CStar.functionalCalculusForm_iff uses true functions of spectral values, not arbitrary occurrence reassignments; use the identity maps for reverse.
C7 | Affine and characteristic polynomial form | LEAN_IFF | MOC.Reformulations.CStar.affineForm_iff and determinantValue_affine, also pointwiseCharacteristicForm_iff. Weight distribution may depend on scalar parameter.
C8 | Universal free product form | LEAN_FINITE_PAIR_IFF; FULL_FREE_PRODUCT_MATH_ONLY | MOC.Reformulations.pairedStarRepresentationForm_iff for pairs of star representations in a common matrix algebra. The exact abstract C-star statement follows by the universal property, but the abstract full C-star free product and quotient are not constructed in Lean.
C9 | Compound (Cauchy-Binet) form | LEAN_IFF | MOC.Reformulations.compoundForm_iff via principal minors and Cauchy–Binet; spectral-pair-dependent projections, not complete minor tables.
C10 | Strong form (compound Birkhoff property) | LEAN_SUFFICIENT; REFUTED | The compound law implies the simultaneous characteristic polynomial law. The order-four arithmetic certificate in the proof map refutes both. The Lean order-five common-law obstruction gives a separate refutation.
C11 | Abelianization convexity principle | DETERMINANT_IFF; SEPARATE_REFUTED; SIMULTANEOUS_REFUTED | abelianizationDeterminantForm_iff handles the determinant in the finite paired representation model. moc_of_separateCoefficientForm gives the top-coefficient implication. firstThreeElementaryCoefficients_weights gives a shared law for indices 1 through 3. The fourth elementary coefficient bound fails in every order at least five by an exact order-five certificate and zero padding. In order four the fourth coefficient is the determinant. The new Lean source awaits kernel verification. The whole characteristic-polynomial law also has an exact order-four counterexample.
S1 | MOC.Claim | ALL_ORDER_IFF | MOC.mocIsTrue_iff_no_proper_paired_blocks: Only orders n>=4 and unitaries without a proper paired block split need be checked.
S2 | MOC.SparseRow | ALL_ORDER_IFF | MOC.mocIsTrue_iff_support_degree_at_least_three: Only n>=4 and unitary mixers with every row and column of support size at least three. This is not a claim that a general maximizer has degree <=2.
S3 | MOC.ReducingCommutant | ALL_ORDER_IFF | MOC.mocIsTrue_iff_regular_scalar_common_commutant: Only n>=4, nonzero cross-sums, injective permutation matching products, and scalar common commutant of the two normal inputs.
S4 | MOC.SpectralGap | FIXED_ORDER_IFF | MOC.conjecture_iff_balanced_nonnormal: Nonempty finite index; unit spectral energy, equal traces and equal cubic moments sum |a_i|^2 a_i, and nonnormal sum suffice.
S5 | MOC.NormalSupportMaximum | ALL_ORDER_IFF | MOC.mocIsTrue_iff_exists_normal_support_maximizer: For n>=4, every pair of spectra and direction admits some unitary global maximizer with normal sum, not that every maximizer is normal.
S6 | MOC.FullSupportReduction | FIXED_ORDER_IFF | MOC.conjecture_iff_regular_spectra_full_support: Unitary has every entry nonzero, every cross-sum nonzero, and all permutation matching products distinct. Density supplies removal of all three restrictions.
S7 | MOC.Source | FIXED_ORDER_IFF | MOC.conjecture_iff_anchored: Select row/column anchors i0,j0. For x_i0=y_j0=0, compare det(U-diag(x)Udiag(y))/det U with products of 1-x_sigma(j)y_j.
S8 | MOC.Support | POINTWISE_IFF | MOC.holds_iff_normalized_support_gaps: For a unitary, the signed weight pairing is nonnegative on all actual spectral gaps that are nonnegative and normalized to sum one.
S9 | MOC.Support | POINTWISE_IFF | MOC.holds_iff_axes_and_pair_normals: For a unitary, only ±1, ±i and normals from ordered pairs of matching values suffice. Axes also handle degenerate hulls.
S10 | MOC.FourMinorTransport | LEAN_ORDER_FOUR_IFF | MOC.conjecture_four_iff_orthogonal; all complex spectra, real orthogonal mixers, n=4 only. Uses a symbolic convex mixture of orthogonal minor tables, not a permutation mixture. Whole coefficient vector also has this reduction (CStar.simultaneousCharacteristic_four_iff_orthogonal).
S11 | MOC.ProjectiveTransport | POINTWISE_IFF | MOC.holds_fractional_iff: Apply a common Mobius map to a and -b; require nonzero 2x2 determinant and no pole on signed spectra. Same unitaries, common nonzero determinant/product factor.
S12 | MOC.FiveNonreal | RESTRICTED_ALL_ORDER_IFF | MOC.hermitianByNormalAtMost_iff_orders_le: For fixed k, Hermitian-by-normal assertions of every order with <=k nonreal partner entries iff the full Hermitian-by-normal case in all orders <=k. Not unrestricted MOC.
